statement='''Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let α,β≥0 satisfy 0<α≤β and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v, and let η>0 with βη≤1. Fix arbitrary y,xRef∈E, z₀=(x₀,p₀)∈E×E and an arbitrary sequence e_n≥0. Define c=y−η∇V(xRef); Φ_t(x,p)=(c+cos(t)(x−c)+√η sin(t)p, −sin(t)(x−c)/√η+cos(t)p); S(x,p)=(x,p−(2⟨p,∇V(x)−∇V(xRef)⟩/‖∇V(x)−∇V(xRef)‖²)(∇V(x)−∇V(xRef))), using total real division, so a zero normal gives the identity; λ(x,p)=√η max(0,⟨p,∇V(x)−∇V(xRef)⟩); H(x,p)=(η⁻¹‖x−c‖²+‖p‖²)/2; C(z)=√η β√(2H(z))(√(2ηH(z))+‖c−xRef‖); Λ_z(t)=∫₀ᵗλ(Φ_s z)ds for t≥0; and τ_z(e)=inf{t≥0:Λ_z(t)≥e}∈[0,∞], with inf∅=∞. Records are the disjoint union of finite active pairs (T,z) and a phase-free stopped symbol †. Define next_e(†)=†; for an active (T,z), put next_e(T,z)=† if τ_z(e)=∞, otherwise next_e(T,z)=(T+τ_z(e),S(Φ_(τ_z(e))z)). Define r₀=(0,z₀), r_(n+1)=next_(e_n)(r_n), and T_n as the finite time coordinate when r_n is active and ∞ when it is stopped. Then: (1) the initial record is exactly (0,z₀); (2) the successor identity holds, and an active record stops at the next index iff its actual clock is infinite, otherwise it has exactly the displayed active successor; (3) next is jointly Borel in y,xRef,e,r; (4) for each n, r_n is jointly Borel in y,xRef,z₀ and the whole threshold sequence; (5) T_n is jointly Borel in the same inputs; (6) T₀=0 and T_n is nondecreasing; (7) a stopped record at n remains stopped at every n+k; (8) if r_n=(T,z), then H(z)=H(z₀), and for every t≥0 with t<τ_z(e_n), H(Φ_tz)=H(z₀) and 0≤λ(Φ_tz)≤C(z₀); (9) C₀=C(z₀)≥0, C₀>0 implies T_n+max(e_n/C₀,0)≤T_(n+1) for every n, including stopped records, while C₀=0 and an active record with e_n>0 imply that the next record is stopped; (10) for an active r_n=(T,z), e_n=0 gives r_(n+1)=(T,S(z)), while e_n>0 and a finite active successor (T′,z′) imply T<T′. All statements concern the actual finite indexed recursion with fixed y,xRef. No iid realization, almost-sure nonaccumulation, single physical-time phase in the presence of zero thresholds, all-time process, Markov law, invariance, terminal sampler or cost theorem is asserted.'''
