 step('Prove joint Borel measurability of one actual successor','On active inputs, compose the jointly Borel clock with the parameter/phase/threshold projections. The finite-value extraction is Borel; the equality-to-infinity guard is Borel. Compose the actual jointly Borel flow and bounce for the finite branch, then use measurable conditional and disjoint-union maps. A measurable product-over-sum equivalence includes the stopped constant branch.',r'(y,x_{\rm ref},e,r)\longmapsto\operatorname{next}_e(r)\text{ is Borel}.','  have hnextmeas :','  have hrecordmeas ('),
 step('Prove joint Borel finite record and event-time maps','Induct on the finite index. The initial map injects (0,z₀); each successor composes the Borel next map with the previous record and the measurable n-th coordinate of the threshold sequence. The event-time map is the disjoint union of the finite time projection followed by extended-time inclusion and the constant ∞ map.',r'(y,x_{\rm ref},z_0,e)\longmapsto r_n\text{ and }T_n\text{ are Borel for every }n.','  have hrecordmeas (','  have henergy ('),
 step('Carry the original energy through every active finite index','Induct on the index, generalizing the candidate active record. At zero the phase is z₀. A stopped predecessor or infinite clock cannot produce an active successor. A finite active successor is SΦ_q(z); flow preservation and bounce preservation give H(SΦ_q(z))=H(z)=H(z₀).',r'r_n=(T,z)\Longrightarrow H(z)=H(z_0),\quad H(S\Phi_qz)=H(\Phi_qz)=H(z).','  have henergy (','  have hmono ('),
 step('Prove nondecreasing event times and stopped absorption','At every successor, stopped records remain stopped and have time ∞. An active record either stops, increasing its extended time to ∞, or adds a nonnegative finite wait. Successor monotonicity gives monotonicity on ℕ. A separate induction on k proves that stopping at n persists at n+k.',r'T_0=0,\quad T_n\le T_{n+1},\quad r_n=\dagger\Rightarrow r_{n+k}=\dagger.','  have hmono (','  have harcs ('),
 step('Use the original energy for every outgoing arc and cap','For an active phase z, combine its inherited H(z)=H(z₀) with H(Φ_tz)=H(z). The actual rate is nonnegative, and the already proved same-energy-layer bound gives λ(Φ_tz)≤C(z₀). Since C depends on phase only through H, it also gives C(z)=C(z₀). The displayed arc conclusion keeps its source t<τ guard.',r'H(\Phi_tz)=H(z_0),\quad0\le\lambda(\Phi_tz)\le C(z_0),\quad C(z)=C(z_0).','  have harcs (','  have hincrement ('),
 step('Derive the uniform extended waiting increment','For C₀>0, the actual clock bound at the current active phase gives τ_z(e_n)≥e_n/C(z). Replace C(z) by the proved C₀, then add the existing finite event time. An infinite next clock gives the extended inequality automatically. Already stopped records have ∞ on both sides, so the inequality remains valid for every n.',r'C_0>0\Longrightarrow T_n+\max\{e_n/C_0,0\}\le T_{n+1}.','  have hincrement (','  have hzerocap ('),
 step('Handle zero original cap with a positive threshold','For an active phase, its proved cap equals C₀. If C₀=0 and e_n>0, the actual one-clock zero-cap law says τ_z(e_n)=∞; the exact active stopping equivalence then makes the successor stopped. This conclusion makes no finite-clock assumption.',r'C_0=0,\ r_n=(T,z),\ e_n>0\Longrightarrow\tau_z(e_n)=\infty\Longrightarrow r_{n+1}=\dagger.','  have hzerocap (','  have hzeroevent ('),
 step('Keep zero thresholds and strict positive finite growth distinct','For e_n=0, the exact clock is zero and Φ_0 is the identity, yielding (T,Sz) at the same event time. For a positive threshold with an active successor, the clock must be finite; its strict positivity gives a strictly positive finite waiting value, hence T<T′. Collect the ten conclusion groups. Repeated zero-threshold times do not define a single physical-time phase or prove nonaccumulation.',r'e_n=0\Rightarrow r_{n+1}=(T,Sz),\qquad e_n>0,\ r_{n+1}=(T^{\prime},z^{\prime})\Rightarrow T<T^{\prime}.','  have hzeroevent (','\nend\n')
